{"id": "q0074", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3813861270, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "A company produces chocolate in bars. In one day, it can produce 5000 bars. The company sells all the produced bars for $2 per bar. How much money will the company receive for selling produced chocolate bars during two weeks?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0074.wav", "input_sha256": "c8466ed485fce9e5d445ba4ff8d9bd6a718173c992aeac6535dd430d530c3b50", "input_samples": 293600, "input_s": 18.35, "n_real_chunks": 19, "score": 0.1877, "act": 0.9982, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Let's break this down. First, we need to figure out how many bars are made in two weeks. The company makes 5, 000 bars each day. There are 7 days in a week, so two weeks have 14 days. That means they produce 5,0 00 times 14 bars, which is 70,0 00 bars total. Now, since each bar sells for $2, we multiply 7 0,000 by 2. So, 7 0,0 00 times 2 equal s 14 0,000 dollars. The company will receive 1 40,0 00 dollars from selling the chocolate bars in two weeks.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 18, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 33, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0074_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "f3971eeb55531eae35d352eada57b834320c6d5e0b6889360802327faf37467d", "sr": 24000, "se