{"id": "q0137", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 536156447, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "What is the smallest real number $x$ in the domain of the function $$g(x) = \\sqrt{(x-3)^2-(x-8)^2}~?$$\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0137.wav", "input_sha256": "86aad970feea5a3456f1b04e0efa075935d88f2e150a9715bf019ffffeef19fc", "input_samples": 139800, "input_s": 8.738, "n_real_chunks": 9, "score": 0.7966, "act": 0.9995, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So the function is defined when both of these are defined. The first one is defined when x squared minus 3x plus 2 is not equal to zero, so we can factor that as x minus 1 times x minus 2. That's not equal to zero, so x is not equal to 1 or 2. And then the second one is defined when 2x minus 8 square d is not equal to zero, so x is not equal to 4. So the domain consists of all real numbers except for 1, 2, and 4. And the smallest of those is 1.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 8, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 34, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0137_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "11a9c935c07e87db2669bdf2a2be9315cf24b8eeaba475c4374fc91429bf9d7c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 33.52}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.06, 1.107, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.063, 2.112, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.064, 3.113, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.064